center",{"title":227,"path":228,"stem":229},"Employee Management","\u002Fdesign\u002Femployee-management","9.design\u002Femployee-management",{"title":231,"path":232,"stem":233},"Player Tracker Rework","\u002Fdesign\u002Fplayer-tracker-rework","9.design\u002Fplayer-tracker-rework",{"title":235,"path":236,"stem":237},"Qualifications","\u002Fdesign\u002Fqualifications","9.design\u002Fqualifications",{"id":239,"title":101,"body":240,"description":605,"extension":606,"links":607,"meta":608,"navigation":609,"path":102,"redirect":607,"seo":610,"stem":103,"__hash__":611},"content_en\u002F1.getting-started\u002F7.reference\u002Fadvanced.md",{"type":241,"value":242,"toc":594},"minimark",[243,247,252,255,284,292,297,339,343,353,356,367,377,381,388,391,402,411,415,421,424,431,435,438,441,445,590],[244,245,246],"p",{},"Use this page when your FiveNet setup goes beyond the basic installation and required configuration options.",[248,249,251],"h2",{"id":250},"common-advanced-topics","Common Advanced Topics",[244,253,254],{},"The most common advanced configuration areas are:",[256,257,258,266,272,278],"ul",{},[259,260,261,265],"li",{},[262,263,264],"strong",{},"Trusted proxies"," when FiveNet runs behind NGINX, Traefik, Cloudflare, or another reverse proxy.",[259,267,268,271],{},[262,269,270],{},"Object storage"," when uploads should be stored in S3-compatible storage instead of the local filesystem.",[259,273,274,277],{},[262,275,276],{},"OAuth2 providers"," when users should be able to authenticate through external identity providers.",[259,279,280,283],{},[262,281,282],{},"Tracing and observability"," for debugging, performance analysis, and distributed request tracing.",[244,285,286,287,291],{},"For the most important option names and config paths, see the ",[288,289,10],"a",{"href":290},".\u002Fconfig-reference",".",[293,294,296],"h3",{"id":295},"tracing-notes","Tracing Notes",[256,298,299,307,314,332],{},[259,300,301,302,306],{},"Set ",[303,304,305],"code",{},"enabled: true"," only after you have a working OTLP endpoint.",[259,308,309,310,313],{},"Use a low ",[303,311,312],{},"ratio"," value in production unless you explicitly want to sample more traffic.",[259,315,316,317,320,321,324,325,328,329,291],{},"Keep the ",[303,318,319],{},"environment"," value aligned with the environment where FiveNet runs, such as ",[303,322,323],{},"development",", ",[303,326,327],{},"staging",", or ",[303,330,331],{},"production",[259,333,334,335,338],{},"Use ",[303,336,337],{},"attributes"," to attach additional metadata that helps identify traces in your observability platform.",[248,340,342],{"id":341},"reverse-proxy-and-trusted-proxies","Reverse Proxy and Trusted Proxies",[244,344,345,346,349,350,291],{},"If FiveNet is deployed behind one or more reverse proxies, review the ",[303,347,348],{},"http.trustedProxies"," option in your ",[303,351,352],{},"config.yaml",[244,354,355],{},"This is especially important when:",[256,357,358,361,364],{},[259,359,360],{},"client IP addresses should be preserved correctly",[259,362,363],{},"FiveNet is running behind NGINX, Traefik, or Cloudflare",[259,365,366],{},"you rely on forwarded headers from trusted infrastructure",[244,368,369,370,373,374,376],{},"See the ",[288,371,10],{"href":372},".\u002Fconfig-reference#http"," for the ",[303,375,348],{}," setting.",[248,378,380],{"id":379},"object-storage","Object Storage",[244,382,383,384,387],{},"By default, FiveNet stores uploads on the local filesystem. For more scalable or externally managed storage, you can switch to S3-compatible object storage through the ",[303,385,386],{},"storage"," configuration.",[244,389,390],{},"This is commonly useful when:",[256,392,393,396,399],{},[259,394,395],{},"running multiple instances",[259,397,398],{},"using cloud infrastructure",[259,400,401],{},"keeping uploaded files outside the application host",[244,403,369,404,373,407,410],{},[288,405,10],{"href":406},".\u002Fconfig-reference#storage",[303,408,409],{},"storage.type"," setting and related storage options.",[248,412,414],{"id":413},"oauth2-providers","OAuth2 Providers",[244,416,417,418,387],{},"FiveNet can be integrated with external authentication providers through the ",[303,419,420],{},"oauth2.providers",[244,422,423],{},"Use this when users should sign in through systems such as Discord or another OAuth2 or OpenID Connect provider instead of relying only on local authentication flows.",[244,425,369,426,373,429,376],{},[288,427,10],{"href":428},".\u002Fconfig-reference#oauth2",[303,430,420],{},[248,432,434],{"id":433},"tracing","Tracing",[244,436,437],{},"FiveNet supports OpenTelemetry-based tracing for the server and worker components. This can help you inspect request flow, background processing, and performance bottlenecks in more advanced environments.",[244,439,440],{},"Tracing is usually only needed when you already have an observability stack in place or when you are troubleshooting more complex issues.",[293,442,444],{"id":443},"example-tracing-configuration","Example Tracing Configuration",[446,447,452],"pre",{"className":448,"code":449,"language":450,"meta":451,"style":451},"language-yaml shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","otlp:\n  enabled: false\n  # otlptracegrpc or otlptracehttp\n  type: \"otlptracegrpc\"\n  # OTLP tracing endpoint URL\n  url: \"https:\u002F\u002Fexample.com:4317\"\n  insecure: false\n  timeout: 10s\n  environment: \"production\"\n  ratio: 0.1\n  attributes:\n    - service.name=fivenet-server\n","yaml","",[303,453,454,467,480,487,505,511,526,536,547,561,573,581],{"__ignoreMap":451},[455,456,459,463],"span",{"class":457,"line":458},"line",1,[455,460,462],{"class":461},"swJcz","otlp",[455,464,466],{"class":465},"sMK4o",":\n",[455,468,470,473,476],{"class":457,"line":469},2,[455,471,472],{"class":461},"  enabled",[455,474,475],{"class":465},":",[455,477,479],{"class":478},"sfNiH"," false\n",[455,481,483],{"class":457,"line":482},3,[455,484,486],{"class":48